This product draws on a sister project of the DSD Toolbox:

- the dsd2pcm quality tools (https://github.com/dsd-toolbox/dsd2pcm-rs, tools/quality),
  Copyright (c) 2026 The dsd2pcm-rs authors, MIT OR Apache-2.0: the Legendre-zero
  modulator design that the reference modulator in src/dsd_measure/encode.py extends
  to higher order, and the table of SoX-DSD filters per DSD rate in
  src/dsd_measure/adapters.py.

Everything else (the reference decoder, the analysers, the C modulator core and the
32-tone multitone, whose phases come from the seeded search in
src/dsd_measure/signals.py) is written for this project.

Methods and measurement practice that this product follows, without taking code from
their authors, are credited in README.md and docs/footprint.md ("Sources and credit").

Third-party tools that dsd-measure runs as separate programs are not part of this
product and are not distributed with it: SoX-DSD (GPL-2.0-or-later), sacd_extract
(GPL-2.0-or-later), ffmpeg (LGPL-2.1-or-later) and SoX (GPL-2.0-or-later). The files
under containers/ only say how to build each one from its own source, and
docs/reference-tools.md names their authors.
